 {\rm (}Swan~\cite{swan, swan2}{\rm )} \label{thm.swan}
Let $G$ be a directed graph with $n$ vertices and $m$ edges. Let $a$ and $b$ be two of the vertices (not necessarily distinct). If $m \geqslant 2n$,
then the number of even Eulerian paths from $a$ to $b$ equals the number of odd Eulerian paths from $a$ to $b$.

